  "properties": {
    "title": "MapStore, a developers introduction",
    "description": "This workshop will provide an introduction to building your own GeoPortal based on the [MapStore Open Source framework](https://mapstore.geosolutionsgroup.com/mapstore/#/).\n\n[MapStore downstream projects](https://docs.mapstore.geosolutionsgroup.com/en/latest/developer-guide/mapstore-projects/) are applications based on [MapStore's WebGIS product](https://github.com/geosolutions-it/MapStore2). They represent the standard best practice for using MapStore as a framework to develop sophisticated WebGIS portals by reusing and extending its core building blocks.\r\nThe workshop provides an overview of the MapStore technological stack and introduces to the development of a MapStore project.\r\n\r\nThe topics covered during the workshop are the following:\r\n- Introduction to MapStore\r\n- How to create a MapStore project\r\n- How to customize the look and feel of a MapStore project \r\n- Configure plugins\r\n- Configure internationalization\r\n- Configure printing\r\n- Extending the MapStore project with your own plugins\r\n\r\nIn order to participate in the workshop a working knowledge of npm, ReactJS and JavaScript is needed.",
